bridge the session bus into the guest, the way pulse already is

muvm forwards X11, PipeWire and PulseAudio and leaves the message bus behind, so
anything in the guest that speaks D-Bus finds nothing. A tray icon is the visible
case: an indicator that cannot reach org.kde.StatusNotifierWatcher falls back to
an XEmbed icon, and an XEmbed icon has no menu.

The mechanism is already here. PulseAudio is bridged with one krun_add_vsock_port
on the host and one setup_socket_proxy in the guest, and the session bus needs
exactly the same pair. The socket lands on the guest's own runtime directory as
"bus", which is where a client looks when DBUS_SESSION_BUS_ADDRESS is unset, so
nothing has to be told about it.

The host side is guarded on the socket existing, as pulse is, so a session
without a bus is unchanged.

Upstream: AsahiLinux/muvm#6 and #187, both open with no maintainer reply.

